Overview
In this lab, you build Code Assist, an internal system that researches production errors for engineers. It is a heterogeneous multi-agent system: its specialist agents are written in different frameworks and run on different Google Cloud runtimes, yet they cooperate as one system by speaking the Agent2Agent (A2A) protocol.

You build the system up one specialist at a time, and the story gets easier at each step:

You start with the Agent Development Kit (ADK) and see how quickly agents-cli deploys an agent to Agent Runtime.
You learn that any framework works over A2A by deploying a LangGraph agent to Cloud Run.
You go faster still with vibecoding: you generate a BigQuery vector-search agent from a prompt using the Antigravity coding agent, then deploy it to GKE.
You compose the specialists as A2A nodes in an ADK 2.0 graph workflow, and test the whole system locally.
You deploy the root to Agent Runtime and register it in Gemini Enterprise.
You extend the running system with one more specialist.
The specialists:

Agent	Framework	Runtime	How you build it
github_agent	ADK + MCP	Agent Runtime	configure + agents-cli deploy
stackexchange_agent	LangGraph + a2a-sdk	Cloud Run	build image + gcloud run deploy
bq-agent	ADK + BigQuery	GKE	generate with Antigravity + agents-cli deploy
manual_search	local ADK tools	Agent Runtime (in the root)	Vertex AI Search datastore + official Google docs (Developer Knowledge MCP, via a Skill Registry skill)
salesforce_agent	ADK + Salesforce REST/SOSL	Cloud Run	configure + agents-cli deploy
code_assistant (root)	ADK 2.0 Workflow	Agent Runtime	orchestrate + agents-cli deploy
System diagram

This is an advanced lab. It assumes you are comfortable with Python, gcloud, containers, and the basics of ADK and multi-agent systems. The default model is gemini-3.5-flash.

Objectives
In this lab, you learn how to perform the following tasks:

Configure and deploy ADK agents to Agent Runtime, Cloud Run, and GKE with agents-cli.
Make agents from different frameworks interoperate over the A2A protocol.
Generate a working agent from a prompt with the Antigravity coding agent.
Orchestrate specialists as A2A nodes in an ADK 2.0 graph workflow and register the system in Gemini Enterprise.
Give an agent long-term, per-user memory with Vertex AI Memory Bank.
