Task 7. Extend the system with the Salesforce agent
In this task, you extend the running system with one more specialist. The Salesforce agent is an ADK agent that searches an organization's document library in Salesforce Files with app-only (2-legged) OAuth, deployed to Cloud Run. You deploy it and rewire the root to include it, which shows how a shared A2A contract lets you grow the system without touching the specialists you already built.

The Salesforce agent authenticates as an application (app-only, 2-legged) through an External Client App, Salesforce's current framework for API integrations (it replaces the classic Connected App). In the following subtasks you create the app, enable the client-credentials flow, and collect the three values the agent needs: SALESFORCE_CLIENT_ID, SALESFORCE_CLIENT_SECRET, and SALESFORCE_DOMAIN.

Create the External Client App
In your Salesforce org, select the setup icon (gear), then select Setup.

In the Quick Find box, enter App Manager, then select App Manager.

Select New External Client App.

New External Client App in the App Manager

For External Client App Name, enter L400 Lab, and for Contact Email, enter your email address. The API name fills in automatically.

In the API (Enable OAuth Settings) section, select Enable OAuth.

For Callback URL, enter https://login.salesforce.com/services/oauth2/callback.

Under Selected OAuth Scopes, add Manage user data via APIs (api) and Perform requests at any time (refresh_token, offline_access).

In the Flow Enablement section, select Enable Client Credentials Flow.

Select Create.

OAuth settings for the External Client App

Enable the client-credentials flow and set the Run-As user
Some client-credentials settings live in the app's policies, not its OAuth settings.

In the Quick Find box, enter External Client App Manager, then select External Client App Manager.

Find your L400 Lab app, select the row dropdown, then select Edit Policies.

Edit Policies for the External Client App

Expand OAuth Policies and find the OAuth Flows and External Client App Enhancements section.

Select Enable Client Credentials Flow.

For Run-As User, enter your Salesforce username. If you do not know it, check the Personal Information page in Setup.

To avoid IP-range rejections from the connector's egress in Lab 2, set IP Relaxation to Relax IP restrictions.

Select Save.

Get the Consumer Key and Secret
Open your app, select the Settings tab, then expand the OAuth Settings section.

Under App Settings, select Consumer Key and Secret.

The Consumer Key and Secret button

Enter the verification code that Salesforce emails you.

Copy the Consumer Key (your SALESFORCE_CLIENT_ID) and the Consumer Secret (your SALESFORCE_CLIENT_SECRET), and save them for the next subtask.

Find your My Domain URL
In the Quick Find box, enter My Domain, then select My Domain.

From the Current My Domain URL field, copy the host, for example orgfarm-f49dce3e51-dev-ed.develop.my.salesforce.com. This is your SALESFORCE_DOMAIN.

Copy the host only. Use the value in Current My Domain URL (not My Domain Name), without the https:// prefix and without any trailing text such as "with partitioned enhanced domains". Save this domain host value (SALESFORCE_DOMAIN) along with your other Salesforce credentials, as it will be needed in the next labs.
