Send a message to the deployed agent. Run this from the project directory, since agents-cli run needs the manifest, and pass the agent's base URL rather than the card URL. This is a native A2A service on Cloud Run, so use --mode a2a.

cd ~/agents/salesforce-agent
agents-cli run --url "${SF_URL}" --mode a2a "ADR-007"
Copied!
Rewire and redeploy the root
Open ~/agents/code-assistant/.env and set SALESFORCE_AGENT_URL to the card URL you just recorded.

Redeploy the root agent to pick up the new specialist.

cd ~/agents/code-assistant
rm -rf .venv
agents-cli deploy --project ${PROJECT_ID} --no-confirm-project --no-wait \
  --update-env-vars "$(grep -v '^#' .env | grep -v '^$' | grep -v '^GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT' | paste -sd,)"
Copied!
Deploy failing with an auth error? If you see service account info is missing 'email' field, your Application Default Credentials lapsed. Run gcloud auth application-default login, then re-run the deploy. If you see a gcloud reauthentication or "no active account" error instead, run gcloud auth login and re-run the deploy. If the failure persists, click Restart in the Cloud Shell toolbar and re-run this task's export block first.
After the deployment succeeds, send a query that the Salesforce document library can answer, and confirm the root now blends Salesforce results with the other sources.

Note: This service is deployed public (like the Stack Exchange agent) because the root's RemoteA2aAgent calls it over A2A without an auth token. A private service would need the caller to send an identity token whose audience is the service URL, plus roles/run.invoker. In the next task, you give this agent long-term memory with Vertex AI Memory Bank.
